#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366808 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b9d90141-bb87-557b-8f42-7d42bba3c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2y+4z-16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366810} {:answer/id #uuid "152ddd87-e22d-58da-85bb-b549e713fa60" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x+4y+3z-10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366811} {:answer/id #uuid "e03a5aca-94df-508f-a37f-bf286cd93f47" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x-3y+z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366812} {:answer/id #uuid "e48a7bda-ef25-5ea3-836f-2a4b00051777" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x+y+2z-11=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366813} {:answer/id #uuid "c0b69228-be90-5f3b-83c0-2b8ff34eb2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x-2y+z-9=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9d90141-bb87-557b-8f42-7d42bba3c91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3x+2y+4z-16=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366810} :answer-field/id #uuid "ab905e04-ebcb-5bbc-8e7d-cdb57e6bb24a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366809}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "843be179-016c-55ad-bf04-357dd9b69f33" :question/math-academy-id "q-102701" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)=xyz-{z}^{2}$, find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes  through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,3,1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,3,1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}(xyz-{z}^{2})\\text{ }k \\\\  & =yz\\text{ }i+xz\\text{ }j+(xy-2z)k \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,3,1) & =(3)(1)\\text{ }i+2(1)\\text{ }j+(2(3)-2(1))k \\\\  & =3\\,i+2\\,j+4k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,3,1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨3,2,4⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y-3,\\,z-1⟩ & =0 \\\\ 3(x-2)+2(y-3)+4(z-1) & =0 \\\\ 3x+2y+4z-16 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186394071 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129079 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "da47f01b-0db0-586f-9d55-5bd4c952afb6" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Tangent to Plane a Level Surface"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "55726bdf-bd92-5f7e-a7bc-7a1d0597e754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394073} {:answer/id #uuid "9575e423-448b-5b5c-91fc-c2a7c6afcec3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394074} {:answer/id #uuid "21a4639b-6da9-5a98-9ba9-dde732cd477b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-3,\\,y+2,\\,z-2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394075} {:answer/id #uuid "14d65a68-8209-56ec-85e3-86c5087733e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨2,-3,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394076} {:answer/id #uuid "6fd689ee-da18-5ee8-8e2e-94f4eb0e8982" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x+2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "55726bdf-bd92-5f7e-a7bc-7a1d0597e754" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394073} :answer-field/id #uuid "1883a36c-4cc8-545f-9348-6c077cb4b1e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186394072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6f18a33a-3190-5d7a-b7c8-c7f2c7cbfe22" :question/math-academy-id "q-80768" :question/problem "Given the function $f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz$,  find the equation of the tangent plane to the level surface that passes through the point where $(x,y,z)=(2,-1,-1).$" :question/worked-solution "The equation of the tangent plane to the level surface $f(x,y,z)=k$ at the point $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ can be expressed as\n\n$$\n∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩=0.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the gradient of $f(x,y,z)$ and evaluate it at $({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})=(2,-1,-1):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇\\,f(x,y,z) & ={f}_{x}(x,y,z)\\,i+{f}_{y}(x,y,z)\\,j+{f}_{z}(x,y,z)\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }i+\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }j+\\frac{∂}{∂z}({x}^{2}y+{y}^{2}-xz)\\text{ }k \\\\  & =(2xy-z)\\text{ }i+({x}^{2}+2y)\\text{ }j-xk \\\\ ∇\\,f(2,-1,-1) & =(\\,2(2)(-1)-(-1)\\,)\\text{ }i+(\\,{2}^{2}+2(-1)\\,)\\text{ }j-2k \\\\  & =-3\\,i+2\\,j-2\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now write down the Cartesian equation of the tangent plane to the level surface, as follows: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})\\cdot ⟨x-{x}_{0},\\,y-{y}_{0},\\,z-{z}_{0}⟩ & =0 \\\\ ∇f(2,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0 \\\\ ⟨-3,2,-2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,\\,y+1,\\,z+1⟩ & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
